o diagnose gestational diabetes  we use the two-step um procedure  that starts with a 50 gram load in the  center  box 50 gram glucose load with one hour  post glucose testing  and depending on their glucose result  after that they can be  negative on the far left swim lane they  could be positive on the far right or  they can be intermediate between 7.8 and  11.  if that happens then they are referred  for a 75 gram glucose tolerance test  where we test post low glucose at one  hour  and two hours but before all of that we  actually do a fasting glucose  and if a fasting glucose or a one hour  post low glucose or a two hour post low  glucose any of them  if they are elevated then gestational  diabetes is diagnosed so i want to draw  your attention  to the fasting glucose greater than or  equal to 5.3  so even before any postflow glucose  testing can be done  we can diagnose gestational diabetes in  these patients  so back to the drink why we  why should the drink not be given well  i've alluded to that  um but first of all um you know it's  actually quite inconvenient for the  patient to have to  consume the drink and then wait around  for two hours on subsequent blood draws  to figure out if they have gestational  diabetes or not  or or just regular diabetes if they're  non-pregnant there's also a certain  amount of discomfort and risk associated  with tolerance testing  there's blood collection that's involved  in pregnant women particularly they're  susceptible to vomiting and nausea  these are the major causes for  cancelling these tests  and there is a small risk of  hyperglycemia or or  post load hypoglycemia due to  overactive beta cells and and a  hyperinsulinemic response  and there's some costs associated with  the lab as well which we're very  cognizant of  being part of a public health care  system in canada there's costs and  consumables there's cost to do the  testing  and there's actual staff being involved  in the testing which prevents  other patie